Package: nchsNatality
Type: Package
Title: Read and Losslessly Pack NCHS Natality Public-Use Files
Version: 0.0.1
Authors@R: person("Vince", "Carey", email = "stvjc@channing.harvard.edu",
    role = c("aut", "cre"))
Description: Reads the fixed-width natality (birth) public-use files from the
    US National Center for Health Statistics using a record layout and value
    labels extracted from the NCHS User Guide. Fields can be returned as typed
    columns or as labelled factors. The whole file can be packed into compact,
    sharded Parquet files from which every record can be rebuilt exactly, with
    a verification step that confirms this.
License: Artistic-2.0
Encoding: UTF-8
Depends: R (>= 4.1.0)
Imports: data.table, vroom, utils
Suggests: DBI, duckdb (>= 1.1.0), testthat (>= 3.0.0), knitr, rmarkdown,
    dplyr, arrow, DT
VignetteBuilder: knitr
Config/testthat/edition: 3
Roxygen: list(markdown = TRUE)
